# recorded data, logs, runtime — never commit
research/data/*
# ...except the one file that says what the data in there MEANS (CRYP-005).
# 861MB of ticks cannot go to GitHub; the declaration of their day boundary must.
!research/data/DAY_BOUNDARY.md
*.log
*.pid

# regenerable sample datasets (make with: python research/make_sample.py)
research/sample_*.csv

# local tooling / OS cruft
.claude/
.DS_Store
__pycache__/

# AUDIT-013 (7), 2026-10-09: BOOK-001 operational state, never data. The flock file beside a shared book (atomicio.hold_book) and the write-beside file a crash
# between write and os.replace can leave (<book>.tmp.<pid>) must not be swept into a commit by a `git add -A` session-end sweep. Same two patterns as stock-radar,
# zero-dte-lab, insider-radar, command-center and asia-radar. (Lock files already tracked stay tracked: ignoring never untracks.)
*.lock
*.tmp.*
